keys-Apple-M5U-TF-Full-GLM5.3-MLX-4bit
Modified copy of TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold) at upstream
tag v1.3.5 (commit 02b324ae9767253d9911d753d5c835a5070eed1b). Releases up to
v0.1.0 of this repository were based on upstream commit d30325dc (1.3.4).

Changes made by this repository's author (drowzeys), 2026, are listed in
MODIFICATIONS.md. In short: a new model family `glm_ax` (full GLM-5.3 on MLX
4-bit weights, Metal, with MTP, DFlash2 and DSpark drafting), its registration in
four upstream files, one dispatch-size fix in the GLM DSA indexer, opt-in
diagnostics and event polling in the Metal 4 queue, upstream's README moved to
README-TensorFold.md, benchmark scripts and an MTP-head merge script under glm53/.

The glm_ax Metal kernels were derived from TensorFold's own GLM-5.3-Flash
kernels (glm_sparse_nax, glm_index_nax and their split/combine decode path) and
build on TensorFold's core row-projection, affine matmul and MoE routing code.
The drafter ports reuse TensorFold's MiniMax-M3 DFlash2/DSpark kernels.

zig/kernels/metal/glm_ax/glm_ax_mpp.metal (prompt attention) contains code adapted
from Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash, commit d23cfa1f, Apache-2.0),
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/listed_attention.metal (attention_bf16_listed_kv1_g64),
which ports the method of oMLX 0.8.0rc1's tensor-unit sparse MLA attention
(https://github.com/jundot/omlx, omlx/patches/glm_moe_dsa/sparse_mla_nax.py,
Apache-2.0). It was changed to read glm_ax's cache rows in place through each row's
key list; its header names both sources.
The DSpark drafter code (glm_ax/dspark.zig) was written from the semantics of
RedHat AI's speculators (DSparkDraftModel) and vLLM's qwen3_dspark / dspark
speculator code (both Apache-2.0), read only, not copied; the DFlash2 drafter
(glm_ax/dflash2.zig) follows SGLang's DFlash2DraftModel (Apache-2.0) the same way.
These changes are released under the same Apache License, Version 2.0.

